{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q413793","formula":"C₂₈H₅₄GdN₅O₂₀","hill":"C28H54GdN5O20","elements":["H","C","N","O","Gd"],"composition":{"C":28.0,"H":54.0,"N":5.0,"O":20.0,"Gd":1.0},"names":{"en":"Gadopentetate dimeglumine"},"descriptions":{"en":"Gadopentetic acid, sold under the brand name Magnevist, is a gadolinium-based MRI contrast agent. It is usually administered as a salt of a complex of gadolinium with DTPA (diethylenetriaminepentacetate) with the chemical formula A2[Gd(DTPA)(H2O)]; when cation A is the protonated form of the amino sugar meglumine the salt goes under the name \"gadopentetate dimeglumine\". It was described in 1981 by Hanns-Joachim Weinmann and colleagues and introduced as the first MRI contrast agent in 1987 by the Schering AG. It is used to assist imaging of blood vessels and of inflamed or diseased tissue where the blood vessels become \"leaky\"."},"fame":10,"pubchemCid":55466,"mass":938.0,"charge":0,"smiles":"CNC[C@@H]([C@H]([C@@H]([C@@H](CO)O)O)O)O.CNC[C@@H]([C@H]([C@@H]([C@@H](CO)O)O)O)O.C(CN(CC(=O)O)CC(=O)[O-])N(CCN(CC(=O)O)CC(=O)[O-])CC(=O)[O-].[Gd+3]","inchikey":"LGMLJQFQKXPRGA-VPVMAENOSA-K","iupac":"2-[bis[2-[carboxylatomethyl(carboxymethyl)amino]ethyl]amino]acetate;gadolinium(3+);bis((2R,3R,4R,5S)-6-(methylamino)hexane-1,2,3,4,5-pentol)","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"55466","atoms":108,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":1.863,"y":0.567,"z":2.617,"el":"C"},{"x":1.033,"y":0.618,"z":1.299,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.365,"y":1.116,"z":1.393,"el":"N"},{"x":-1.275,"y":0.105,"z":1.984,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.575,"y":-1.046,"z":1.017,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.359,"y":-0.978,"z":0.073,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.929,"y":-2.206,"z":1.279,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.427,"y":2.406,"z":2.151,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.81,"y":3.13,"z":2.057,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.6